<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>ISO 3166 codes</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">ISO 3166 codes</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>ISO 3166</strong> defines the country and subdivision codes used in ISO 20022 addresses: <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> must carry a two-letter <strong>ISO 3166-1 alpha-2</strong> code (exactly <code>[A-Z]&#123;2&#125;</code>), and <code>&lt;CtrySubDvsn&gt;</code>, where used, must carry an <strong>ISO 3166-2</strong> subdivision code such as <code>US-CA</code> or <code>GB-ENG</code> under the CPMI harmonised model.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How ISO 3166 codes works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>Codified country values are what make field-level sanctions screening possible: engines match <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> against sanctioned jurisdictions directly instead of pattern-matching free text — the root cause of false positives like "Cuba Street" triggering Cuba alerts. The ISO 3166-2 requirement standardises subdivision naming for uniform downstream parsing.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §3.2 / §4.6; CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §4 footnote / p6-4; Appendix I Q7.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
